# Zero- Flow preset — no dedicated graphics card: any Intel or AMD laptop or desktop
# that uses built-in graphics (Intel UHD / Iris Xe, AMD "Radeon Graphics").
#
# Apply it:  python check_hardware.py --apply        (merges into your .env)
#   or copy this file to .env — anything not listed here keeps its normal default.
#
# Speed, measured on an 8-core i7-11700: large-v3 needs 12.8 s for a 14 s clip on the
# CPU — too slow — and the voice runs at 3x real time. "small" is about six times
# lighter than large-v3 (estimate: 2-3 s per clip). With 8 GB of RAM or less, use
# "base" and gemma2:2b — check_hardware.py does that for you.

WHISPER_MODEL_NAME="small"        # "base" with 8 GB RAM or less
WHISPER_DEVICE="cpu"              # skip the GPU attempt: there is no NVIDIA card
OLLAMA_MODEL_NAME="qwen2.5:3b"    # "gemma2:2b" with 8 GB RAM; run `ollama pull` first
READER_DEVICE="cpu"               # the voice on the CPU (starts after ~1 s per sentence)
